# Check a credential is valid

You can check a credential is valid by looking at its:

* [certificate path](#certificate-path)
* [status information](#status-information)

You must not trust a credential with errors in its credential status or certificate pathway. 

## Certificate path

You can check a credential's validity by inspecting its full certificate path back to its Issuing Authority Certificate Authority (IACAS). 

The procedure is laid out in section 9.3 of the [ISO/IEC 18013-5 specification](https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/en/#iso:std:iso-iec:18013:-5:ed-1:v1:en) for a mdoc credential. This covers areas of validation including:

- certificate signatures 
- expiration dates 
- certificate usage constraints
- name constraints
- certificate revocation lists (CRLs) following [RFC 5280](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc5280#section-6)


## Status information 

You can use the Status List Service to [check a live credential’s status](statuslist/index.html) information. This will tell you whether the credential is valid or revoked.






